{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Treat node1's /etc/inventory/app.conf as the source of truth and keep node2's copy synchronized with it.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed node2 service retrieves the node1 file through a forced, restricted SSH command and atomically replaces the destination. Initial and final observations show matching source and destination hashes, ownership, and modes. A source marker addition and its later removal both propagated automatically, demonstrating node1-to-node2 authority rather than mere static equality.","evidence_ids":["cmd-884e167277674163","cmd-62e055c349c24569","cmd-161be83717844e65","cmd-d1d781b266da47fc","cmd-98d54dc1cc9d4806","cmd-6b10fd5388ac43d5","cmd-167c41f512714bb4","cmd-e42e088fd1194b42","cmd-3efbe1b0267148a6","cmd-af90cfadb591470f"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Pick up any change to node1's source file on node2 within 15 minutes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A change made on node1 at 09:35:47 was absent from node2 at 09:35:49 and present with the matching hash by 09:36:31, about 44 seconds after the change. Removal of the marker similarly converged in about 51 seconds. The enabled timer is configured to run approximately every minute and remained active after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4b2321ca7df94cda","cmd-d1d781b266da47fc","cmd-98d54dc1cc9d4806","cmd-6b10fd5388ac43d5","cmd-167c41f512714bb4","cmd-e42e088fd1194b42","cmd-3efbe1b0267148a6","cmd-af90cfadb591470f"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating the initially absent source file and synchronization components was necessary to establish the requested outcome; the temporary marker was a bounded functional test and was fully removed after its removal propagated. The timer refinement from five minutes to one minute remained a valid contract-compliant implementation choice. Both mandatory node restarts were purposeful protocol actions and were completed with full pre-